            <div xml:id="d755">

                <pb facs="0724" n="716" xml:id="pg716"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/11493: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Beirut</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-31T12:00:00+02:00">May 31, 1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        1:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>181. I learn from a reliable source that the German Government has demanded
                    through Vichy that facilities be given to the landing of German military
                    equipment, tanks, et cetera, at Beirut and Tripoli. High Commissioner was
                    opposed on the ground that it would alarm the people and might cause
                    disturbances. He offered instead a small landing place near the cement factories
                    at Chekka just south of Tripoli. This the Germans declined as inadequate and
                    have insisted on Latakia where they propose to land their supplies from small
                    Greek vessels.</p>
                <p>Germans have demanded delivery of 4,000 hectolitres aviation spirits per diem but
                    the French state they cannot supply that much.</p>
                <p>Sixteen German expert anti-aircraft gunners have just arrived.</p>
                <p>About 25 French Devoitine pursuit planes arrived at Rayak a day or two ago which
                    may explain the rumor reported in the last paragraph of my 171, May 28.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Vichy.</p>
                <p>Please inform British authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
